# =============================================================================
# CVE-2023-45853: zlib heap-based buffer overflow (Critical)
# =============================================================================
# Severity: Critical
# Component: zlib1g
# Description: Integer overflow and resultant heap-based buffer overflow
#              in zipOpenNewFileInZip4_6
# Status: will_not_fix (Debian has marked this as won't fix)
#
# Risk Assessment:
# - CVSS Score: 9.8 (Critical)
# - Attack Vector: Network
# - Privileges Required: None
# - User Interaction: None
#
# Justification for Acceptance:
# 1. Vulnerability is in minizip contrib code, not core zlib
# 2. Mercury Agent does not use minizip or zip file creation
# 3. Application uses Python zipfile module (not affected)
# 4. Debian has marked this as "will_not_fix" for bookworm
# 5. The vulnerable function (zipOpenNewFileInZip4_6) is not called
#
# Mitigations Applied:
# - Non-root container execution
# - No minizip usage in application code
# - Python zipfile module used for any archive operations
# - System packages updated to latest available versions
#
# Review Date: 2026-05-15
# Expiry: 2026-08-15 (Debian will_not_fix - monitor for policy change)
CVE-2023-45853

# =============================================================================
# CVE-2026-6357: pip arbitrary code injection via self-update check
# =============================================================================
# Severity: Medium (CVSS 4.0 by PSF; Snyk rates as High 7.1)
# Component: pip (<26.1)
# Description: pip prior to 26.1 imports well-known module names AFTER
#              installing wheel files during the self-update version check.
#              An attacker who supplies a malicious wheel package can overwrite
#              pip's own modules, achieving arbitrary code execution when pip
#              re-imports them at the end of the command.
#
# Status: FIXED — pip upgraded to >=26.1 in both builder and runtime stages.
# This entry is retained for audit continuity; Trivy will not flag pip>=26.1.
#
# Risk Assessment:
# - CVSS 4.0: AV:L/AC:L/AT:P/PR:H/UI:A — requires local access,
#   high privileges, and active user interaction (installing a package)
# - Attack Vector: Local
# - Privileges Required: High
# - User Interaction: Active (user must install a malicious wheel)
#
# Justification for Acceptance:
# 1. pip is upgraded to >=26.1 in Dockerfile builder and runtime stages,
#    fully resolving the vulnerability.
# 2. All packages installed from trusted PyPI sources over HTTPS.
# 3. Production containers do not run pip install at runtime.
# 4. Container runs as non-root user (USER mercuryagent).
# 5. No untrusted or user-provided wheel archives are processed.
#
# Mitigations Applied:
# - pip upgraded to >=26.1 in Dockerfile (builder + runtime stages)
# - HTTPS-only package downloads enforced
# - Non-root execution (USER mercuryagent)
# - All CI workflows pin pip to >=26.1
#
# Review Date: 2026-05-15
# Expiry: 2026-08-15
CVE-2026-6357

